note Rosetta Code task "Knapsack problem/Unbounded": https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Knapsack_problem/Unbounded
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
om2
text nl "\n"
text sp " "
text minus "-"
text thead "panacea ichor gold value weight volume\n"
text ttenth "/10 "
text tthou "/1000\n"
note emit writes every byte of a to stdout; a short write is retried, an error exits 1
fn emit a view uchar * to void
o = ulong 0
while lt o len a bound 4096
k = write 1 a o sub len a o
if le k 0
exit 1
end
o = add o ulong k
end
end
note emitu writes n in decimal; 20 digits hold every ulong
fn emitu n ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
i = ulong 20
v = n
while true bound 20
i = sub i 1
put d i uchar add rem v 10 48
v = div v 10
if eq v 0
break
end
end
emit part d i sub 20 i
end
note the weights are in tenths (0.3, 0.2, 2.0 -> 3, 2, 20; limit 25 -> 250) and the volumes in
note thousandths (0.025, 0.015, 0.002 -> 25, 15, 2; limit 0.25 -> 250), so all arithmetic is exact;
note values are 3000, 1800 and 2500; every count that fits is tried (at most 11 * 17 * 13 cases)
fn fits a ulong b ulong c ulong to bool
w = add add mul a 3 mul b 2 mul c 20
v = add add mul a 25 mul b 15 mul c 2
ret and le w 250 le v 250
end
fn value a ulong b ulong c ulong to ulong
ret add add mul a 3000 mul b 1800 mul c 2500
end
fn row a ulong b ulong c ulong to void
emitu a
emit sp
emitu b
emit sp
emitu c
emit sp
emitu value a b c
emit sp
emitu add add mul a 3 mul b 2 mul c 20
emit ttenth
emitu add add mul a 25 mul b 15 mul c 2
emit tthou
end
note pass 1 finds the best value, pass 2 prints every combination that reaches it
fn main to int
best = ulong 0
for a ulong 11
for b ulong 17
for c ulong 13
if fits a b c
if gt value a b c best
best = value a b c
end
end
end
end
end
emit thead
for a ulong 11
for b ulong 17
for c ulong 13
if fits a b c
if eq value a b c best
row a b c
end
end
end
end
end
ret 0
end
